<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Molina</h1><p class="st-meta">1129 CE – 1293 CE (approx.) · capital Molina de Aragón</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A semi-independent Castilian lordship on the borders of Aragon, ruled by the Lara family and governed by its own celebrated fuero.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-i-of-aragon">Alfonso I of Aragon</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/molina-de-aragon">Molina</a> around 1129. It was soon granted to the Castilian noble <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manrique-perez-de-lara">Manrique Pérez de Lara</a>, who held it under Castilian overlordship and in 1154 gave the town and its land a fuero, a charter of rights for settlers.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/molina-de-aragon">Molina</a> was a frontier lordship of herders and settlers between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and Aragon, defended by its great castle. Its lords issued laws and raised troops with considerable autonomy. In the 13th century the heiress Mafalda married the infante <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-de-molina">Alfonso de Molina</a>, brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-of-castile">Ferdinand III</a>, tying it closer to the Castilian royal family.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blanca-alfonso-de-molina">Blanca Alfonso de Molina</a> died childless in 1293, and the lordship passed to her half-sister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-de-molina">María de Molina</a>, queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sancho-iv-of-castile">Sancho IV</a>, and thus to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/crown-of-castile">Crown of Castile</a>. Spanish kings still bear the title Lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/molina-de-aragon">Molina</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 1129 CE – 1293 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region